From d6dd137f2fdadb3eda35bcb2f2a0764ee14d8b5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Boettcher <pboettcher@anduril.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:57:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] nvethernet: add SIOCGHWTSTAMP support

issue: facing an unsupported ioctl error while
launching the ptp4l, since get timestamp configuration
support is not there.

fix: add get timestamp configuration ioctl support

Bug 5274698
Bug 5287071

Change-Id: I9254b041d4d3b9dc2cddebc14dc6100ed1b76807
Signed-off-by: Narayan Reddy <narayanr@nvidia.com>

[ Backported from linux-nv-oot commit 38227b2177ae4f23e5e0a0ed59bb180837f95d71,
  which is present on the rel-38 / JetPack 7 line but was never backported to
  rel-36. Depends on the cached pdata->ptp_config added by the preceding patch.

  The original also amends an ioctl list in a doc comment in
  ether_callback_export.h. rel-36 has no such file -- its export header is
  ether_export.h and carries no such list -- so that hunk is dropped. ]

Signed-off-by: Peter Boettcher <pboettcher@anduril.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c
index aae8157..0cff29f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c
@@ -3885,6 +3885,7 @@ static int ether_ioctl(struct net_device *dev, struct ifreq *rq, int cmd)
 	int ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	struct ether_priv_data *pdata;
 	struct mii_ioctl_data *mii_data;
+	struct hwtstamp_config *config;
 
 	if (!dev || !rq) {
 		pr_err("%s: Invalid arg\n", __func__);
@@ -3953,7 +3954,10 @@ static int ether_ioctl(struct net_device *dev, struct ifreq *rq, int cmd)
 	case SIOCSHWTSTAMP:
 		ret = ether_handle_hwtstamp_ioctl(pdata, rq);
 		break;
-
+	case SIOCGHWTSTAMP:
+		config = &pdata->ptp_config;
+		ret = copy_to_user(rq->ifr_data, config, sizeof(*config)) ? -EFAULT : 0;
+		break;
 	default:
 		netdev_err(dev, "%s: Unsupported ioctl %d\n",
 			   __func__, cmd);
